This is an official Melius UI-only template.

Preserve existing data-melius-ui-id and data-melius-ui-role values unless the user explicitly asks to rename visual editor metadata.
Do not add data-melius-id, data-melius-form, data-melius-action, or data-melius-view in the template source by default.
Do not add src/melius.app-spec.json, src/melius.client.ts, or src/melius.actions.ts to the template source.

Template direction:
Fixed-sidebar design studio portfolio inspired by a local reference project named vessel-studio. Keep the desktop split layout with a 30% fixed left sidebar, a thin dashed vertical divider, and a 70% right work column with large 4:3 project cards. On tablet use a wider 40% sidebar, and on mobile let the sidebar stack above the project list.

Preserve the quiet light-gray sidebar, near-white work surface, compact logo mark, large direct headline, two rounded CTA buttons, horizontal trusted-company ticker, rotating testimonial, large image-led work cards with hover overlay, presentational contact form, and oversized faint footer wordmark. The baseline uses a sample brand, sample copy, and replaceable stock imagery rather than protected third-party brand assets.

The baseline includes Japanese/English copy switching plus explicit light/dark mode switching. Preserve the in-page language and theme toggles unless the generated app intentionally removes them. The selected language and theme should persist in localStorage and document.documentElement.lang / data-theme should stay in sync. Query parameters locale, lang, language, melius_locale and theme, themeMode, colorScheme, melius_theme must override localStorage in previews.

If the user asks for saving forms, contact delivery, project detail pages, case-study CMS, authentication, notifications, payments, or other platform behavior, add the required Melius App Spec and data-melius-* bindings during the generated app editing flow, not as part of the UI-only template baseline.
Keep UI styling editable by the visual editor: use static Tailwind className strings on real HTML elements inside the template UI kit. Do not use style props, CSS-in-JS, cn/clsx/twMerge, or complex dynamic className construction.
Keep forms visually complete, but treat them as presentational UI until Melius bindings are added later.
